mullion (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Screen edge switching:
    - New default "Show a button" mode: reaching the edge next to the other
      computer shows a "Switch to …" pop-up; nothing changes unless it is
      clicked. The previous behaviour is "Switch when pushed".
    - Push mode needs a firmer push (300 px by default), adjustable as
      Push Strength (Light, Medium, Firm), and the pointer must then stay
      at the edge for half a second, so a quick flick doesn't switch.
    - The edge is ignored while a mouse button is held, near the corners
      (top panel, Activities corner, bottom 48 px) and for 3 s after the
      keyboard and mouse arrive.
    - "mullion cross <edge> --check" tells whether an edge leads to the
      other computer.
    - Edge events are logged to the journal.
  * Extension behaviour checks in make check.

 -- Ante Karamatic <ivoks@ubuntu.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:43:38 +0100

mullion (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
    - GTK 4 / libadwaita UI and CLI for controlling monitors over DDC/CI.
    - Input selection, side swap, second input.
    - Screen layouts: single, 50/50, 75/25, 80/20, 25/75, 20/80 and two
      picture-in-picture sizes.
    - KVM (USB hub) switching with state detection via USB.
    - Optional GNOME custom keyboard shortcuts.
    - Original GPL-3+ application icon.
    - Translations with gettext; Croatian translation.
    - Hand over the keyboard and mouse at the screen edge (GNOME Shell
      extension).
    - Brightness, contrast and volume sliders and commands.
    - GNOME on-screen pop-up for shortcut and screen-edge actions.
    - Unit tests (make check) and GitHub Actions CI.
    - Monitor tile in GNOME Quick Settings.

 -- Ante Karamatic <ivoks@ubuntu.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:29:29 +0100
